files: CLAUDE.template.md, claude.yml, settings.template.json, quarantine.template.md, agent-auditor.template.md, archive/claude-0.1.0.yml, archive/claude-0.1.0-checkout-v7.yml
updated: 2026-08-07
changelog: |
  0.4.0 — FF-0020 + FF-0021: two OPT-IN agent artifacts (never in the default
  artifact set), amending the 0.3.0 position: hooks/skills/commands/agents
  still never fan out by default — dedicated, explicitly-requested kit
  artifacts are the sanctioned exception.
  (1) quarantine.template.md (artifact `claude-guardrails`) → .claude/skills/
  _shared/quarantine.md: the canonical shared guardrails doc (untrusted-input
  quarantine, honesty rule, merge discipline), reconciled strictest-wins from
  lifehacker.dev's _shared/quarantine.md and the inline boilerplate in the
  Jekyll trio's agents. Agents cite it in one line instead of restating.
  (2) agent-auditor.template.md (artifact `claude-agent-auditor`) → .claude/
  agents/agent-auditor.md: parameterized meta-auditor (accuracy/consistency/
  least-privilege drift audit, one PR or none), merged from it-journey's
  agent-auditor and lifehacker.dev's agent-reviewer; seeded only when NO
  auditor-role agent exists — hand-authored auditors are never touched.
  0.3.1 — claude.yml bumps actions/checkout to v7, matching the mechanical
  bump that already reached 27 fleet copies (which made them non-byte-identical
  to the 0.1.0 archive and invisible to --upgrade). archive/ gains the
  claude-0.1.0-checkout-v7.yml variant so --upgrade recognizes BOTH machine
  shapes (pristine 0.1.0, and 0.1.0 + the checkout bump); anything else is
  treated as hand-modified and left alone.
  0.3.0 — three changes:
  (1) settings.template.json: an optional minimal .claude/settings.json baseline
  (artifact `claude-settings`) — the schemastore $schema plus a universally-safe
  read-only permissions allowlist (git status/log/diff, gh pr view, gh run view).
  DECLARED POSITION on fleet .claude/ directories: the kit seeds ONLY this
  settings baseline. Hooks, skills, commands, agents, and agent memory are
  repo-specific and never fan out — repos that need them grow them locally.
  Conventions for locally-grown layers: python3 fail-open hook payload parsing
  (exit 0 when a dependency is missing), kebab-case frontmatter names, no
  `model:` pins unless a role demonstrably needs one, namespace command names
  to avoid collisions with hub commands (e.g. /evolve), and keep user-scoped
  memory out of repos (user facts belong in ~/.claude, not committed
  agent-memory).
  (2) Seeded files now carry a `kit: agent-context vX.Y.Z` stamp
  (__KIT_VERSION__ substituted by fanout.sh) so version drift is detectable.
  (3) archive/claude-0.1.0.yml: byte-exact copy of the 0.1.0 claude.yml, used
  by `tools/fanout.sh --upgrade` to safely refresh machine-seeded, unmodified
  copies. CORRECTION to the 0.2.0 note below: the concurrency block reached
  ZERO fleet repos — 36 of 37 seeded copies verified byte-identical to 0.1.0
  (the 37th, bashcrawl, was hand-modified and is skipped by --upgrade).
  0.2.0 — claude.yml gains a per-thread `concurrency` group (cancel-in-progress:
  false) so concurrent @claude mentions serialize instead of racing each other on
  the same branch. NOTE: the kit is additive-only, so repos that already
  carry a seeded claude.yml do NOT pick this up via fan-out — they need the
  block applied via --upgrade (see 0.3.0).
  0.1.0 — initial kit.
notes: CLAUDE.template.md is seeded only when the target has NO agent-context file (CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md/copilot-instructions/.cursorrules); claude.yml only when .github/workflows/claude.yml is absent; settings.template.json only when .claude/settings.json is absent. All additive-only, never overwrite — except `--upgrade`, which replaces a claude.yml ONLY when it is byte-identical to archive/claude-0.1.0.yml (machine-seeded, never touched).
